@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@*
    The application layout. A <main> landmark and the routed page inside it, and nothing else yet.

    <main> is here rather than in index.html because it has to wrap the ROUTED content: a landmark
    around the pre-boot placeholder would announce an empty region, and a screen-reader user
    skipping to the main landmark expects to land on the page they navigated to.

    WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. No context bar, no Space switcher, no Role chip, no navigation
    and no account menu. Story 1.4 built Sessions, so a person can now be signed in - and there is
    still nothing for a chrome to DISPLAY, because a Session carries no Space and no Role by
    design (AC1), and the Host's Space-scoped endpoints are not yet called from here. Story 1.7 owns the
    context bar and AccountScopedContext, and is the story that gives this layout something to
    hold. A placeholder header now would be a component that story has to unpick.

    NO SIGN-OUT CONTROL EITHER, and its absence is a recorded decision rather than an oversight.
    No FR, CAP, journey or acceptance criterion in the artifact set asks for sign-out - yet
    UX-DR31 names it as one of the five purge triggers, which presupposes it exists. Story 1.4
    raised it as a question for Lee and assigned the purge seam's extension to story 1.7, which is
    also the story that builds the bar such a control would live in.

    There is no skip link either, for the original reason: a skip link needs something to skip
    PAST, and today the main landmark is still the first thing on the page.
*@

<main>
    @Body
</main>
